## Slice 2: Runtime Core Orchestration

- Date: 2026-05-31
- Plan reference: docs/plan.md §2.2
- Status: PASSED (all tests green; first full run after authoring passed)

### Objective
Build the development manager (supervisor state machine), phase DAG/registry,
retry/escalation controls, checkpoint lifecycle, event bus, run summary, and the
twelve phase-agent stubs.

### Files created
core/:
- core/phase_dag.py            (PhaseDAG: linear pipeline, ready_phases, downstream_of, cycle validate — FR-SV-005)
- core/phase_registry.py       (PhaseRegistry: phase->contract lookup)
- core/retry_controller.py     (RetryController: 2-retry budget, 2s exp backoff — FR-SV-018, NFR-RB-002)
- core/escalation_service.py   (EscalationPacket + EscalationService.escalate — FR-SV-019/020)
- core/development_manager.py  (DevelopmentManager supervisor: start/dispatch/run_until_pause,
                                gate pause+approval, retries->escalation, rollback, resume — FR-SV-006..023)
state/:
- state/__init__.py
- state/event_bus.py           (EventBus: JSONL append + subscribe/stream — FR-SV-024/026)
- state/checkpoint_store.py    (CheckpointStore + PhaseCheckpoint: save/load/invalidate/earliest_invalid_phase — FR-SV-021/022A)
- state/run_summary.py         (RunSummaryWriter: human-readable per-phase log — FR-SV-025)
agents/:
- agents/factory.py            (PhaseAgentFactory.create(phase_id) — blueprint §3.1)
- agents/phase_invocation.py   (build_invocation_payload + stub_phase_result)
- agents/phases/__init__.py + 12 phase agents (proposal..cleanup), deterministic stubs

Tests:
- tests/unit/runtime/test_phase_dag.py
- tests/unit/runtime/test_retry_controller.py
- tests/unit/runtime/test_checkpoint_store.py
- tests/unit/runtime/test_development_manager.py
- tests/unit/runtime/test_event_bus.py          (added: subscribe/stream coverage)
- tests/integration/phase_flow/test_secure_gate_pause.py
- tests/integration/phase_flow/test_resume_with_invalid_checkpoint.py
- tests/e2e/checkpoint_resume/test_resume_after_restart.py

### Test results
- `python -m pytest tests` → 76 passed (48 from Slice 1 + 28 new).
- Coverage (`--cov=anvil_runtime`): 95% overall.
  - core aggregate ≈93% (dev_manager 90%, escalation 100%, dag 100%, retry 100%,
    registry 76%); state aggregate ≈91% (checkpoint 92%, event_bus 98%,
    run_summary 86%). Both clear the ≥85% targets; overall clears ≥70%.

### Design decisions (within blueprint/spec, no drift)
- Phase DAG is the linear 12-phase pipeline (each phase depends on its
  predecessor), executed serially in topological order (proposal §8.6,
  architecture §686). Declaration is parallel-ready.
- Phase agents are deterministic success stubs in v0.1.0; real OpenHands-backed
  execution replaces `stub_phase_result` in Slice 5 without changing the
  `payload -> PhaseCompleteEvent` contract (plan §3.3 "phase agent stubs").
- Result/orchestration models not pinned to a specific file by the blueprint
  (RunProgress, PhaseDispatchResult, ApprovalDecision, RollbackPlan, ResumePlan,
  EscalationPacket, PhaseCheckpoint) were defined inside their already-assigned
  matrix modules — no new module files were introduced (no drift vs plan §8).
- Secure gates: post-proposal/post-architecture/post-blueprint fire AFTER their
  phase; pre-deployment fires BEFORE the deployment phase (proposal §7). YOLO
  skips user-facing gates but keeps internal controls (FR-OM-002).

### Issues encountered and fixes
- None functionally; all suites passed on the first full run. After the initial
  green run, added test_event_bus.py and a failing-agent escalation test to
  exercise the retry->escalation path (FR-SV-017/019), which the success-only
  stubs did not cover. Raised overall coverage 91% -> 95%.

### Drift check (against blueprint / architecture / spec)
- Modules created == the Slice-2 rows of the plan §8 assignment matrix
  (core/{development_manager,phase_dag,phase_registry,retry_controller,
  escalation_service}; agents/{factory,phase_invocation,phases/*};
  state/{event_bus,checkpoint_store,run_summary}). No unmapped modules.
- state/event_bus.py is shared with Slice 6 (completeness/redaction pass later);
  Slice 2 implements emit/subscribe/stream only, as planned.
- No drift detected.

### Carry-forward
- Phase agents are stubs (no real artifact authoring) until Slice 5; therefore
  FR-SV-009 artifact-existence enforcement and FR-SV-010 drift checks are
  intentionally deferred to Slice 6 (artifacts/validator, drift/checker).
- The TypeScript extension still requires Node.js to run its vitest suite (see
  Slice 1 carry-forward); unchanged by Slice 2 (runtime-only).

