## Slice 3: Config, Runtime Projection, Policy, and Hooks

- Date: 2026-05-31
- Plan reference: docs/plan.md §2.3
- Status: PASSED (all tests green)

### Objective
Implement effective configuration resolution (4-level precedence), runtime
projection writing, policy enforcement + remediation, and lifecycle hook
enforcement.

### Files created
config/:
- config/loader.py       (ConfigLoader + ConfigSources; reads 4 levels, YAML errors per FR-CF-007)
- config/merger.py       (ConfigMerger + deep_merge: scalar override / list union / deep map — FR-CF-001/002/003)
- config/validator.py    (ConfigValidator: version + consistency checks — FR-CF-004/006)
- config/projection.py   (RuntimeProjectionWriter + ProjectionManifest: .openhands/runtime/*, hooks.json, logs/)
policy/:
- policy/rule_evaluator.py (RuleEvaluator + PolicyActionContext/PolicyViolation: whitelist/numeric-limit/list-mandatory)
- policy/remediation.py    (Remediator + RemediationOutcome: switch-to-allowed-model — FR-PL-008)
- policy/engine.py         (PolicyEngine + PolicyDecision: check/apply_remediation/enforce — FR-PL-004/005/007)
hooks/:
- hooks/__init__.py
- hooks/lifecycle_hooks.py (HookKind/HookRule/HookDecision/TokenUsage + matchers — spec §4.2.2)
- hooks/compiler.py        (HookCompiler -> .openhands/hooks.json)
- hooks/adapter.py         (HookAdapter: before/after tool+prompt, allow/deny/mutate + audit)

Tests:
- tests/unit/runtime/test_config_merger.py        (merge semantics, loader, validator)
- tests/unit/runtime/test_projection_writer.py
- tests/unit/runtime/test_policy_engine.py
- tests/unit/runtime/test_hook_adapter.py
- tests/integration/policy/test_forbidden_model_remediation.py
- tests/integration/policy/test_hook_enforcement.py
- tests/e2e/security_profile/test_restricted_policy_flow.py

### Test results
- `python -m pytest tests` → 106 passed (30 new).
- Coverage (`--cov=anvil_runtime`): 94% overall.
  - config aggregate ≈96%, policy aggregate ≈90%, hooks aggregate ≈93% — all
    clear the ≥85% targets where applicable; overall clears ≥70%.

### Design decisions (within blueprint/spec, no drift)
- List-union merge preserves lowest-precedence-first order with de-duplication,
  matching the FR-CF-002 worked example exactly.
- Projection writes mcp.generated.json + policy-snapshot.json (blueprint §6.1)
  and delegates hook compilation to HookCompiler (.openhands/hooks.json,
  spec §4.2.2); manifest carries content checksums for reproducibility.
- Policy v0.1.0 supports the three spec-defined rule families (whitelist /
  numeric-limit / list-mandatory). `switch-to-allowed-model` is the implemented
  remediation strategy; unremediable violations return no outcome so the
  supervisor escalates (FR-PL-005).
- Helper contracts (ConfigSources, ProjectionManifest, PolicyActionContext,
  PolicyViolation, RemediationOutcome, PolicyDecision, HookRule, HookDecision,
  TokenUsage) were defined inside their already-assigned matrix modules — no new
  module files introduced (no drift vs plan §8).

### Issues encountered and fixes
- None functionally; suites passed on the first full run. Added two follow-up
  tests (validator consistency guards; list-mandatory gate rule) to cover real
  branches that the happy-path tests skipped.

### Drift check (against blueprint / architecture / spec)
- Modules created == the Slice-3 rows of the plan §8 assignment matrix
  (config/{loader,merger,validator,projection}; policy/{engine,remediation,
  rule_evaluator}; hooks/{adapter,compiler,lifecycle_hooks}). No unmapped modules.
- config/schema.py and policy/models.py (Slice 1) were consumed, not modified.
- No drift detected.

### Carry-forward
- Policy/hook engines are standalone and event-bus-aware but are not yet wired
  into the DevelopmentManager dispatch path; that integration occurs alongside
  the API surface (Slice 4) and OpenHands adapter (Slice 5).
- MCP server projection writes the resolved server list; live MCP discovery +
  tool authorization is Slice 5 (tools/*).
